isn't funny, all right?

256
00:10:40,181 --> 00:10:42,309
If I wanted the cake
to be a disaster,

257
00:10:42,350 --> 00:10:44,060
I would have
baked it myself.

258
00:10:44,102 --> 00:10:48,315
Uh... is it okay that I still
think it looks delicious?

259
00:10:50,650 --> 00:10:53,069
Jack, look at this.

260
00:10:53,111 --> 00:10:55,905
I know what you're thinking,
Judy.

261
00:10:55,947 --> 00:10:58,283
The resemblance is uncanny.

262
00:11:00,160 --> 00:11:04,456
I am this close to tugging
on my testicles again.

263
00:11:06,082 --> 00:11:08,502
No, no, this is not
what I ordered, okay?

264
00:11:08,543 --> 00:11:10,753
I went all the way
to New Jersey

265
00:11:10,795 --> 00:11:13,340
so that I could have
the perfect cake

266
00:11:13,381 --> 00:11:15,300
for my daughter's birthday,

267
00:11:15,342 --> 00:11:17,718
and I need a bunny cake
right now!

268
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:19,762
Ask them if it
would be faster

269
00:11:19,804 --> 00:11:22,474
if we cut the baby's
face off the penis

270
00:11:22,516 --> 00:11:24,725
so we could put
it on the bunny.

271
00:11:24,767 --> 00:11:27,395
That is a weird sentence.

272
00:11:27,437 --> 00:11:30,982
Oh, believe you me, I am going
to bring this cake back.

273
00:11:31,024 --> 00:11:33,109
I don't even want it
in my home.

274
00:11:33,151 --> 00:11:34,110
Joey, don't touch it!

275
00:11:34,152 --> 00:11:36,488
I'm so confused!

276
00:11:36,530 --> 00:11:39,533
Yes, yes, I still want
my daughter's picture,

277
00:11:39,574 --> 00:11:40,950
but on a bunny cake.

278
00:11:40,992 --> 00:11:43,870
Yellow cake, chocolate frosting,
with nuts.

279
00:11:43,911 --> 00:11:45,872
To be fair, this
one does have nuts.

280
00:11:52,045 --> 00:11:53,963
Hey, Mon, it was really nice
of you to loan Rachel

281
00:11:54,005 --> 00:11:56,049
your car so she could
go get the cake.

282
00:11:56,090 --> 00:11:58,218
It was so nice of her
to pull my hair

283
00:11:58,259 --> 00:11:59,678
till I dropped the key.

284
00:11:59,718 --> 00:12:02,514
Well, you know what,
while we're waiting,

285
00:12:02,556 --> 00:12:05,141
you guys could tape your message
to Emma

286
00:12:05,183 --> 00:12:06,267
for her 18th birthday, huh?

287
00:12:06,309 --> 00:12:07,435
Okay...

288
00:12:07,477 --> 00:12:08,520
Hi, Emma.

289
00:12:08,562 --> 00:12:09,770
It's the year 2020.

290
00:12:09,812 --> 00:12:12,399
Are you still
enjoying your nap?

291
00:12:14,817 --> 00:12:18,071
We're Aunt Monica and Uncle
Chandler by the way.

292
00:12:18,112 --> 00:12:19,738
You may not recognize us

293
00:12:19,780 --> 00:12:23,451
because we haven't spoken to
your parents in 17 years.

294
00:12:23,493 --> 00:12:25,078
We used to be married.

295
00:12:25,119 --> 00:12:27,664
But we missed
a weekend away together

296
00:12:27,706 --> 00:12:30,083
and things kind
of unraveled.

297
00:12:30,124 --> 00:12:31,209
Because of you.

298
00:12:31,251 --> 00:12:33,127
Happy birthday.

299
00:12:33,169 --> 00:12:35,088
MONICA:
Ross, Rachel promised us

300
00:12:35,129 --> 00:12:36,631
it would
be over by now.

301
00:12:36,673 --> 00:12:39,175
We seriously have to go if we
want to get to Vermont.

302
00:12:39,217 --> 00:12:41,928
I called and the last train
leaves in a half hour.

303
00:12:41,969 --> 00:12:43,597
You know, I have
a massage client soon.

304
00:12:43,638 --> 00:12:44,847
You guys,

305
00:12:44,889 --> 00:12:46,600
just please,
a little bit longer.

306
00:12:46,641 --> 00:12:49,894
I promise Rachel will be back
with the cake any minute.

307
00:12:49,936 --> 00:12:51,854
Monica, remember the frosting?

308
00:12:51,896 --> 00:12:55,774
All right,
five more minutes.

309
00:12:55,816 --> 00:12:57,944
( phone ringing )

310
00:12:57,985 --> 00:12:58,945
Hello.

311
00:12:58,986 --> 00:13:02,574
Oh, no. What happened?

312
00:13:02,616 --> 00:13:04,909
Okay, okay, where are you?

313
00:13:04,951 --> 00:13:07,203
Okay, I'll be right there.

314
00:13:07,245 --> 00:13:08,996
Was that Emma? Is she up?

315
00:13:09,997 --> 00:13:11,625
Rachel got pulled over
for speeding.

316
00:13:11,666 --> 00:13:14,127
She forgot her license, so now
I have to bring it to her.

317
00:13:14,168 --> 00:13:16,879
Well, if you're leaving,
I'm definitely going to go.

318
00:13:16,921 --> 00:13:19,633
Wait, if anybody
gets to go, it's us.

319
00:13:19,674 --> 00:13:22,385
We've been complaining
the longest.

320
00:13:22,427 --> 00:13:24,929
Wait, you guys,
you can't leave, okay.

321
00:13:24,971 --> 00:13:26,264
Rachel already

322
00:13:26,306 --> 00:13:27,724
feels bad that the cake's
messed up.

323
00:13:27,766 --> 00:13:29,517
How do you think
she's going to feel

324
00:13:29,559 --> 00:13:31,810
when she comes back here
and all you guys are gone?

325
00:13:31,852 --> 00:13:32,895
I don't know.

326
00:13:32,937 --> 00:13:34,606
You'll tell us on Monday.

327
00:13:34,648 --> 00:13:36,691
Joey, you're in charge,

328
00:13:36,733 --> 00:13:38,234
okay?

329
00:13:38,276 --> 00:13:39,736
Make sure nobody leaves.

330
00:13:39,778 --> 00:13:41,070
Got it.

331
00:13:42,447 --> 00:13:44,991
Hey, hey, hey,
where do you think you're going?

332
00:13:45,032 --> 00:13:47,201
To the bathroom?

333
00:13:47,243 --> 00:13:49,496
All right. Well, the rest
of you get comfortable, okay?

334
00:13:49,537 --> 00:13:51,706
Because we're going to
be here for... Wait a minute...

335
00:13:51,748 --> 00:13:52,957
There's a window in there.

336
00:13:52,999 --> 00:13:55,042
Oh, no. He's not
getting away that easy.

337
00:13:56,544 --> 00:14:00,548
CHANDLER:
What are you doing?!
Get the hell out of here!

338
00:14:06,805 --> 00:14:10,099
Well, that one did not
have Emma's face on it.

339
00:14:10,141 --> 00:14:11,142
No, it did not.

340
00:14:11,184 --> 00:14:12,185
No.

341
00:14:12,226 --> 00:14:14,187
Well, we'd better
get going.

342
00:14:14,228 --> 00:14:15,689
It's late.

343
00:14:15,730 --> 00:14:17,816
Jack's not allowed
to drive at night anymore.

344
00:14:17,856 --> 00:14:19,651
He has trouble staying
in his lane.

345
00:14:19,693 --> 00:14:21,653
Last winter I went up
on a church lawn

346
00:14:21,695 --> 00:14:23,697
and drove right through
a manger scene.

347
00:14:23,738 --> 00:14:25,782
The papers thought it was
a hate crime.

348
00:14:29,410 --> 00:14:30,704
Anyway, it was lovely

349
00:14:30,745 --> 00:14:31,954
seeing you.

350
00:14:31,996 --> 00:14:33,373
Okay.
Bye.

351
00:14:33,414 --> 00:14:34,624
Nighty-night.

352
00:14:34,666 --> 00:14:35,958
Nighty-night.

353
00:14:37,752 --> 00:14:39,754
Joey, how could you just
let them leave?

354
00:14:39,796 --> 00:14:41,881
Hey, hey, hey, I'm not
going to mess with Jack.

355
00:14:41,922 --> 00:14:43,842
He's a great man.
He fought for our country.

356
00:14:43,882 --> 00:14:45,426
No, he didn't.

357
00:14:45,468 --> 00:14:47,387
He pretended to be a
Quaker to get out of Korea.

358
00:14:47,428 --> 00:14:48,388
( gasps )

359
00:14:48,429 --> 00:14:49,806
Well, that's it.

360
00:14:49,848 --> 00:14:52,141
He's the last one to go.

361
00:14:52,183 --> 00:14:54,018
I'm locking you guys in!

362
00:14:54,060 --> 00:14:56,646
You do know I can just turn them
the other way around, right?

363
00:14:56,688 --> 00:15:00,400
Oh, I forgot you used
to live here.

364
00:15:00,441 --> 00:15:02,402
( phone ringing )

365
00:15:05,154 --> 00:15:06,406
Hello.

366
00:15:06,447 --> 00:15:08,241
Joey, it's Estelle.

367
00:15:08,282 --> 00:15:09,492
Hey.

368
00:15:09,534 --> 00:15:11,786
So how'd your
audition go today?

369
00:15:11,828 --> 00:15:13,079
What audition?

370
00:15:13,120 --> 00:15:15,081
The one I told you
about last week.

371
00:15:15,122 --> 00:15:17,458
What?! You never said anything
about an audition!

372
00:15:21,003 --> 00:15:22,547
Let me start over.

373
00:15:22,589 --> 00:15:25,675
I just got a call
about an audition.

374
00:15:25,717 --> 00:15:28,428
I think you can still make it.

375
00:15:28,469 --> 00:15:30,221
It's down at the Astor Theater.

376
00:15:30,263 --> 00:15:32,599
And you need to have
a monologue prepared.

377
00:15:32,640 --> 00:15:34,893
A monologue? I don't have a...

378
00:15:38,479 --> 00:15:39,980
I got it.

379
00:15:40,022 --> 00:15:44,110
Uh, so... I'm going
to take off.

380
00:15:44,151 --> 00:15:45,278
PHOEBE:
What?!

381
00:15:45,319 --> 00:15:46,905
No way. You don't
get to leave!

382
00:15:46,945 --> 00:15:48,155
I've got a massage client

383
00:15:48,197 --> 00:15:50,199
waiting outside my door
any minute.

384
00:15:50,241 --> 00:15:53,369
And we paid for a room
that we're supposed
to be in right now!

385
00:15:53,411 --> 00:15:54,537
Okay, now.

386
00:15:54,579 --> 00:15:57,665
Only one of us has
to stay with Emma.

387
00:15:57,707 --> 00:16:01,168
Okay, and as the person
who realized that, I get to go.

388
00:16:01,210 --> 00:16:02,962
No, no, no.

389
00:16:03,003 --> 00:16:06,340
Let's figure out a
fair way to decide
who's staying.

390
00:16:06,382 --> 00:16:08,092
Oh, I got it.

391
00:16:08,134 --> 00:16:10,804
Okay, everyone pick a
number from one to ten.

392
00:16:10,845 --> 00:16:13,389
All right, whoever gets the
highest number,

393
00:16:13,431 --> 00:16:14,515
gets to go first.

394
00:16:16,183 --> 00:16:17,811
Okay, ten.

395
00:16:17,852 --> 00:16:19,604
Okay, Monica's picks ten.
I call nine.

396
00:16:19,646 --> 00:16:20,647
Anyone else?

397
00:16:22,106 --> 00:16:24,108
Let's just... let's just
draw straws.

398
00:16:24,150 --> 00:16:26,986
Or we flip a coin,
and then multiply
the answer...

399
00:16:27,027 --> 00:16:27,987
I'm begging you, stop.

400
00:16:28,028 --> 00:16:30,364
Okay.

401
00:16:30,406 --> 00:16:31,908
Okay, how about this?

402
00:16:31,950 --> 00:16:33,992
We got wind-up toys for
Emma for her birthday.

403
00:16:34,034 --> 00:16:35,286
We can make them race

404
00:16:35,328 --> 00:16:36,955
and whoever comes
in last, stays.

405
00:16:36,996 --> 00:16:39,373
Yeah! Let's do that!

406
00:16:39,415 --> 00:16:40,750
That sounds more fun

407
00:16:40,792 --> 00:16:42,460
than the thing we were
going to do in Vermont.

408
00:16:42,502 --> 00:16:43,878
Okay, everybody pick a toy.

409
00:16:43,920 --> 00:16:44,879
Okay.

410
00:16:44,921 --> 00:16:46,213
I want the dolphin!

411
00:16:46,255 --> 00:16:47,214
That's a bear.

412
00:16:47,256 --> 00:16:49,216
I'm too excited!

413
00:16:50,217 --> 00:16:52,052
Okay, Phoebe,
you get the bear,

414
00:16:52,094 --> 00:16:53,638
Joey, you get the robot,

415
00:16:53,680 --> 00:16:55,515
and Chandler and I
get the dog.

416
00:16:55,556 --> 00:16:56,766
And the race

417
00:16:56,808 --> 00:16:59,059
is going to go from here
to here.

418
00:16:59,101 --> 00:17:01,187
Now the one who
comes in last

419
00:17:01,228 --> 00:17:03,523
stays.

420
00:17:03,564 --> 00:17:05,859
Okay, ladies and gentlemen,
wind your toys.

421
00:17:05,900 --> 00:17:07,652
On your mark...

422
00:17:07,694 --> 00:17:09,153
get set... go!

423
00:17:09,195 --> 00:17:10,154
Go! Go!

424
00:17:10,196 --> 00:17:11,531
Come on, robot!

425
00:17:11,572 --> 00:17:13,574
( mechanical barking )

426
00:17:13,616 --> 00:17:15,952
What are you barking at?!

427
00:17:21,916 --> 00:17:24,627
Well, how is that
going to help?!

428
00:17:24,669 --> 00:17:26,086
I bought you!

429
00:17:26,128 --> 00:17:28,840
How did I forget that
that's all you do?!

430
00:17:28,882 --> 00:17:31,342
Way to go, robot!

431
00:17:31,384 --> 00:17:34,178
Good job, Alan!

432
00:17:34,220 --> 00:17:35,638
Hey, good race, you guys.

433
00:17:35,680 --> 00:17:36,890
Yeah. See you later.

434
00:17:36,931 --> 00:17:38,933
Oh, no, no, no. Wait.

435
00:17:38,975 --> 00:17:40,727
We didn't lose.

436
00:17:40,768 --> 00:17:43,062
The rules clearly stated
that the last one

437
00:17:43,103 --> 00:17:45,272
to cross the finish line
was the loser.

438
00:17:45,314 --> 00:17:47,775
Well, our dog never
crossed the finish line,

439
00:17:47,817 --> 00:17:48,776
so technically...

440
00:17:48,818 --> 00:17:50,028
They left.

441
00:17:56,242 --> 00:17:58,077
No, there isn't time
to go to the bakery.

442
00:17:58,118 --> 00:17:59,495
We're just going to come home.

443
00:17:59,537 --> 00:18:00,830
Everybody left?

444
00:18:00,872 --> 00:18:03,249
All right, well,
just tell Emma

445
00:18:03,290 --> 00:18:05,919
that we'll be there
as soon as we can.

446
00:18:05,960 --> 00:18:07,378
Bye.

447
00:18:08,713 --> 00:18:09,672
Rachel!

448
00:18:09,714 --> 00:18:11,131
Oh, God! Sorry.

449
00:18:11,173 --> 00:18:13,259
I can't believe they
gave you a ticket.

450
00:18:13,300 --> 00:18:14,802
You're such a good driver.

451
00:18:15,803 --> 00:18:18,765
Emma's awake.

452
00:18:18,806 --> 00:18:19,933
Yeah?

453
00:18:19,974 --> 00:18:21,726
I can't believe this.

454
00:18:21,768 --> 00:18:24,144
It's her first birthday,
she's awake,

455
00:18:24,186 --> 00:18:25,605
we're not even there.

456
00:18:25,646 --> 00:18:27,147
Everybody left.

457
00:18:27,189 --> 00:18:29,442
We've still have this stupid,
obscene cake.

458
00:18:29,483 --> 00:18:31,235
Well, maybe I can fix that.

459
00:18:31,277 --> 00:18:34,154
You know, try to turn it
into something else.

460
00:18:34,196 --> 00:18:35,406
Oh, don't even bother.

461
00:18:35,448 --> 00:18:37,658
We've already ruined her
first birthday.

462
00:18:37,700 --> 00:18:41,203
Do you know how
important these early
experiences are, Ross?

463
00:18:41,245 --> 00:18:44,331
Very, according to the back
cover of that book

464
00:18:44,373 --> 00:18:45,750
that you gave me.

465
00:18:45,792 --> 00:18:48,335
Rach, she's not going
to remember this.

466
00:18:53,132 --> 00:18:55,259
I just had such an idea

467
00:18:55,301 --> 00:18:59,097
of what this day would be like,
you know.

468
00:18:59,138 --> 00:19:03,434
Emma laughing and everybody
gathered around her cake,

469
00:19:03,476 --> 00:19:05,519
singing "Happy Birthday,"

470
00:19:05,561 --> 00:19:07,021
And then we would
all go into...

471
00:19:07,063 --> 00:19:09,148
Get off the road,
you stupid student driver!

472
00:19:09,189 --> 00:19:11,567
( horn honking )

473
00:19:11,609 --> 00:19:13,277
They have to learn!

474
00:19:15,195 --> 00:19:16,155
Hey.

475
00:19:16,196 --> 00:19:17,156
What?

476
00:19:17,197 --> 00:19:18,157
It isn't that bad.

477
00:19:18,198 --> 00:19:19,158
Oh my God.

478
00:19:19,199 --> 00:19:21,159
You made it into a bunny.

479
00:19:21,201 --> 00:19:23,079
How did you do that?

480
00:19:23,121 --> 00:19:25,623
Well, I just made
these two

481
00:19:25,665 --> 00:19:28,001
things cheeks.

482
00:19:28,042 --> 00:19:29,877
And then I...

483
00:19:29,919 --> 00:19:33,547
I split this to make ears.

484
00:19:33,589 --> 00:19:36,342
Well, I'm very impressed.

485
00:19:36,383 --> 00:19:38,218
Some can sing, some can dance,

486
00:19:38,260 --> 00:19:42,140
I, apparently, can turn phallic
cakes into woodland creatures.

487
00:19:44,183 --> 00:19:48,896
Now, another way to organize
your stuffed animals is by size.

488
00:19:48,938 --> 00:19:52,150
I'm sorry, is this a game
for Emma or for Monica?

489
00:19:52,191 --> 00:19:54,152
Game?

490
00:19:54,193 --> 00:19:56,154
Emma,

491
00:19:56,195 --> 00:19:59,365
do you even know it's
your birthday today?

492
00:19:59,406 --> 00:20:01,367
You're one. One year old.

493
00:20:01,408 --> 00:20:02,493
That's little.

494
00:20:02,535 --> 00:20:04,162
( gurgling )

495
00:20:04,203 --> 00:20:05,412
( gasps )

496
00:20:05,454 --> 00:20:07,581
That's my girl.

497
00:20:07,623 --> 00:20:10,751
That's how old you are.

498
00:20:10,793 --> 00:20:12,378
Did I teach her that?

499
00:20:12,419 --> 00:20:14,380
Did I just impart wisdom?

500
00:20:16,924 --> 00:20:18,968
I want one.

501
00:20:19,010 --> 00:20:20,845
Me, too.

502
00:20:24,765 --> 00:20:26,893
There's no one around.

503
00:20:26,934 --> 00:20:29,896
Why don't we just
take this one?

504
00:20:29,937 --> 00:20:31,731
And head to Canada.

505
00:20:31,772 --> 00:20:32,732
I was kidding.

506
00:20:32,773 --> 00:20:34,316
I wasn't. Let's get going.

507
00:20:35,568 --> 00:20:38,196
Hey, are Ross and Rachel back?

508
00:20:38,236 --> 00:20:39,488
No, not yet.

509
00:20:39,530 --> 00:20:41,407
Oh good, I didn't
miss the party.

510
00:20:41,448 --> 00:20:43,576
What about
your massage client?

511
00:20:43,617 --> 00:20:45,327
I just felt so bad missing this,

512
00:20:45,369 --> 00:20:48,081
so I just slipped him
a little something, you know.

513
00:20:48,122 --> 00:20:50,290
As long as I'm back in five
or six hours,

514
00:20:50,332 --> 00:20:51,375
it'll be all right.

515
00:20:53,044 --> 00:20:57,882
Okay, if Ross and Rachel ask,
I've been here the whole time.

516
00:20:57,924 --> 00:20:59,175
The whole time.

517
00:21:00,300 --> 00:21:02,929
I've been here the whole time.

518
00:21:02,970 --> 00:21:05,264
Joey, we just saw you come in.

519
00:21:05,305 --> 00:21:07,683
You ran past us on the stairs.

520
00:21:07,725 --> 00:21:09,227
